 mesa_june:{ask:'June wears three aprons because nobody knows where the diner schedule ends and the repair rota begins.',offer:'Help June hand over the repair desk',help:'You sort desk tasks from trained repairs and write a rota. June eats squash cornbread while someone else answers the bicycle bell.',listen:'You sit down with June between trains. She admits she has been looking at a catering course in the next town.',returnHelp:'The shared rota held through a late train. June has put the course application on the counter instead of hiding it in a drawer.',returnListen:'June taught two neighbors the repair desk herself. She says your conversation made the course feel like an ordinary possibility.',plan:'Apply for catering training while the shared rota keeps the town served.',later:'June has sent the application. Whatever the answer, she now has a Thursday she can call her own.'},
 mesa_inez:{ask:'Inez can spend a small grant on a grand garden launch or repair the leaky irrigation already here.',offer:'Help Inez document the small repairs',help:'You record the leaks and the water they waste. The repair request is unglamorous, specific and hard to dismiss.',listen:'You ask Inez which option the gardeners would still thank her for in a dry month. She puts the launch poster aside.',returnHelp:'The patched irrigation uses less water. Inez gives you the old leak list with every line crossed out.',returnListen:'The gardeners chose repairs over the launch. Inez says it took more meetings and fewer heroic promises.',plan:'Fund irrigation repairs and preserve a water-wise seed library.',later:'Inez has new seeds to lend and enough patience to ask for them back next season.'}
