 if(n.stage==='unmet')return[
  make('neri_accept','Meet Neri over a half-restored map','Neri, 29, restores maps for work and keeps their own travel plans. Spend a quiet hour getting to know each other. This is an introduction, not a partnership.', 'Neri shows you a coastline that an earlier restorer drew too neatly. You compare the places each of you calls home. They ask to talk again next week, after you have both had ordinary days of your own.',{stage:'introduced'},{companionBond:1,joy:5,discoverRegions:['saffron'],revealPlaces:['TRANSIT']},'companion'),
  make('neri_decline','Choose your own route kindly','Tell Neri you are not looking for a shared journey. No relationship penalty; all independent routes remain available.','Neri thanks you for being clear. They still plan to apply for the island posting and leave a useful route suggestion. A warm conversation can be complete without becoming a romance.',{stage:'declined'},{joy:3},'declined')];
 if(n.stage==='introduced')return[
  make('neri_plan_coast','Make a small coastal plan together','Compare work schedules and agree on one possible coastal visit. Neri explains why restoring working maps matters to them. Your home and job stay yours.','Over a creased ferry timetable, you agree that a visit should fit both your work weeks. Neri admits they miss having someone ask how a difficult day went. A shared route now saves $30 on non-Alder fares.',{stage:'planned',plan:'coast'},{companionBond:1,joy:6,discoverRegions:['saffron']}),
  make('neri_plan_home','Make room for each other at home','Tell Neri you want to keep your local commitments. Plan a weekly conversation and a map-restoration afternoon instead of promising a trip.','Neri listens to why these streets matter to you. You agree on an unhurried afternoon and an honest conversation each week. Staying begins to feel like a choice you can share, rather than an apology.',{stage:'planned',plan:'home'},{companionBond:1,joy:6})];
 if(n.stage==='planned')return[
  make('neri_distance','Support the posting and try some distance','Neri has accepted work in Pelagia starting next week. They will go because the work matters. You can keep your home and agree on a realistic rhythm of calls.','Neri says they would regret turning down the restoration work. You say what you would miss, then agree on one call a week rather than constant availability. Neither life has to disappear to keep this possibility open.',{stage:'discussed',challenge:'distance',posting:'accepted'},{companionBond:1,discoverRegions:['pelagia']}),
  make('neri_visit',visitedPelagia?'Build on the visit, without promising a move':'Promise a visit, without promising a move',visitedPelagia?'You have already reached Pelagia. Talk about what meeting around Neri’s work made possible; future visits and any relocation remain separate decisions with visible costs.':'Neri has accepted the Pelagia posting. Agree to visit when your time and cash allow. Travel and any relocation remain separate decisions with visible costs.',visitedPelagia?'You talk about the Pelagia visit you have actually made, then leave the next journey in pencil. Neri does not ask you to abandon your home, and you do not ask them to abandon the posting. A kept visit can become a shared memory without turning into an obligation to move.':'You circle a possible ferry week in pencil. Neri does not ask you to abandon your home, and you do not ask them to abandon the posting. The visit will be a promise to care for, not proof you owe someone.',{stage:'discussed',challenge:'visit',posting:'accepted'},{companionBond:1,discoverRegions:['pelagia']}),
  make('neri_friends','Keep a friendship with separate futures','Care about Neri’s posting while being honest that a romance is not the future you want.','Neri is disappointed for a moment, then relieved to have a clear answer. You trade addresses and keep the possibility of friendship, without either of you waiting for a different answer.',{stage:'discussed',challenge:'friendship',posting:'accepted'},{joy:3,discoverRegions:['pelagia']})];
 if(n.stage==='discussed')return[
  ...(n.challenge!=='friendship'?[make('neri_partner','Choose a relationship, with an actual plan','After several different weeks, decide together to be partners. Your agreement leaves room for the Pelagia posting and your own commitments. It does not relocate you.',`You return to the hard parts of the conversation before saying yes. ${n.challenge==='visit'?(visitedPelagia?'You have made the visit to Pelagia. It gave both of you a real ordinary day to build on; future journeys still need honest plans.':'The first visit is still in pencil; neither of you pretends money and time do not matter.'):'The weekly call has a place in both calendars, with permission to reschedule honestly.'} You choose each other with two lives still visible.`,{stage:'committed',commitment:'partner'},{companionBond:1,joy:8},'partner')]:[]),
  make('neri_friendship','Choose the friendship you can keep','Keep the shared history and choose friendship. This is a worthwhile ending to the question, with no lost route or punishment.','You decide to remain friends. Neri shows you the first photograph from the posting, and asks about the life you are building. The answer makes room for both futures.',{stage:'committed',commitment:'friendship'},{joy:6},'companion')];
 if(n.stage==='committed')return[make('neri_payoff',n.commitment==='partner'?'Keep the first ordinary promise':'Make time for a friend’s news',n.challenge==='visit'&&!visitedPelagia?'You have not made the visit yet. Use this hour to talk honestly and agree to a call while saving for the ferry; the promise can be revised without pretending it happened.':'Give the relationship an ordinary hour after the big decision. Hear about Neri’s first difficult restoration and tell them what changed in your own week.',state(p)!.region==='pelagia'?'You meet after Neri’s shift, away from the famous domes. They show you an awkward repair that will help real ferry crews. The conversation is smaller than a grand arrival and feels like something you could keep doing.':n.challenge==='visit'&&!visitedPelagia?'You say plainly that the visit has to wait. Neri tells you they would rather know than be quietly left waiting. You revise the plan and spend the hour on a real call; care has become something practical.':visitedPelagia?'You call after returning from Pelagia, and both remember the ordinary day you spent there. Neri describes the next difficult map repair; you tell them what changed back home. The kept visit has become shared history rather than a test you must repeat.':'On the first unhurried call, Neri describes a map repair that went wrong. You tell them about your own imperfect week. Neither of you has to make the story more impressive. The ordinary promise holds.',{stage:'fulfilled'},{companionBond:1,joy:10})];
